## Program Outcome

Tool Shed removes only obsolete generated legacy sources through an exact, recovery-proven,
revision-accounted retirement transaction while preserving every file-owned and recovery surface.

## M1-RETIREMENT-SCOPE — Freeze exact scope and managed semantics

Status: active
Depends on: none

Outcome: Produce a deterministic retirement plan from the verified conversion ledger, classify
every inbound path reference, define preserved classes, and add managed alias-retirement plus
read-only dry-run behavior.

Gate:

- `G1-RETIREMENT-SCOPE-FROZEN`: the plan names all and only eligible generated sources, reports
  source/hash/alias drift, classifies every inbound reference, refuses unresolved entries, and
  proves that file-owned and recovery surfaces cannot enter the deletion set.

Candidate campaign: `freeze-safe-legacy-retirement-scope-and-tooling`.

## M2-RECOVERY-REHEARSAL — Prove current recovery and disposable deletion

Status: active
Depends on: M1

Outcome: Generate a current rollback export, verify the external archive, rebuild the current
checkpoint, and execute the exact retirement transaction in a disposable maintainer copy.

Gate:

- `G2-RETIREMENT-RECOVERY-PROVEN`: rehearsal preserves the semantic database digest and current
  document bodies, leaves zero active aliases for deleted sources, produces no broken required
  references, restores successfully from current recovery truth, and passes focused plus full
  validation.

Candidate campaign: `rehearse-and-qualify-legacy-collateral-retirement`.

## M3-CANONICAL-RETIREMENT — Apply the owner-authorized exact manifest

Status: blocked-pending-owner-authorization
Depends on: M2

Outcome: Retire the approved source aliases and delete the exact obsolete generated files in the
canonical maintainer, update deliberate references, checkpoint/rebuild, and qualify the resulting
repository.

Gate:

- `G3-CANONICAL-RETIREMENT-QUALIFIED`: the owner explicitly authorizes the exact manifest and
  retention window; apply is hash-, revision-, identity-, and token-fenced; rollback remains
  available; no excluded class changes; full validation and Doctor pass; Git records only the
  approved retirement scope and required supporting changes.

Candidate campaign: `apply-and-qualify-canonical-legacy-retirement`.

## Authority Boundary

M1 and M2 are reversible planning, implementation, and validation work covered by the current
authority envelope. M3 deletion is destructive and cannot begin until the owner reviews and
explicitly authorizes the exact final manifest, blast radius, archive retention duration, and
rollback procedure.

## KISS Boundary

Use one retirement manifest contract and one guarded implementation path. Do not introduce a
server, dual-write mode, generalized repository cleaner, or unrelated `.tool-shed/` purge.

